  "member_id": "pearce-mark",
  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B003",
        "laureates": [
          "Hidetoshi Katori",
          "Jun Ye"
        ],
        "citation": "for the invention and realization of optical lattice clocks"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B051",
    "B035"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. Optical lattice clocks remain the strongest bounded instrument-led achievement: the magic-wavelength lattice principle and its realization created a reproducible new regime of time and frequency measurement. The decisive test of an experimental advance is that independent groups can make it work and use it as a reliable physical probe; by that standard the platform is mature. Katori and Ye provide a compact, complementary account of originating principle and foundational realization. The prize should recognize that achievement itself, without depending on a future standards decision or on every application that the resulting precision may enable.",
    "case_against": "The principal reservation remains historical boundary. A final account must distinguish the lattice-clock architecture from optical-frequency-comb infrastructure, later international accuracy improvements, and the wider optical-metrology enterprise. We should not let exceptional present performance substitute for evidence that two individuals alone capture the original prizeable chain. Nor should the citation imply that a redefinition of the second or all proposed fundamental applications has already occurred.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "olsson-eva",
        "point": "Olsson argues that aberration-corrected electron optics opened durable, atomic-scale experimental access, but identifies unresolved allocation among correction concepts, practical implementations, and engineering teams.",
        "response": "I agree with the scientific force of B051; it is the closest alternative because it is a genuinely door-opening measurement technology whose capability is demonstrated beyond doubt. But the unresolved attribution is central to the awardable unit, not a drafting detail. Until the proposed trio can be shown to delimit the decisive theory-to-working-instrument chain without arbitrary exclusions, B003 is the more secure final configuration."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "danielsson-ulf",
        "point": "Danielsson favors inflation because its account of primordial structure has broad observational force, while recognizing unresolved microphysics and the absence of confirmed distinctive signatures.",
        "response": "The explanatory ambition and observational programme of B011 are formidable. Yet its remaining discrimination problem matters: the proposed citation must not overstate what observations establish about inflation's physical origin. In B003, the core phenomenon is directly realized, calibrated, and reproduced. That more bounded connection between principle, apparatus, and demonstrated result gives it priority, even though lattice clocks should not claim prospective downstream consequences."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "mehlig-bernhard",
        "point": "Mehlig emphasizes the mature universality of KPZ while questioning whether a prize for the original formulation can credit Spohn alongside Kardar and Zhang while omitting Parisi.",
        "response": "I accept that B022 has the depth and maturity of a major physical idea. The tension he identifies, however, goes directly to the definition of the achievement and the exact credit. B003 has an analogous but narrower historical task: establish the boundary around lattice clocks and then credit Katori and Ye only for that bounded achievement. On the current record its proposed attribution is substantially clearer."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether the historical record can demonstrate that Katori and Ye alone adequately represent the original lattice-clock principle and foundational realization, separately from optical-frequency-comb infrastructure and later community advances.",
      "How a final citation can state the demonstrated physical and metrological advance without absorbing later record-setting performance or prospective applications.",
      "Whether further attribution review of B051 could resolve its competing correction-concept and implementation claims sufficiently to alter the comparison."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "None apparent from the supplied profile. My experimental astroparticle background creates no disclosed collaboration, institutional connection, or other conflict with the proposed laureates."
  }
}
